## Beyond Root

#### With root Access


I can also just use my root shell on the host to check out the web directory, and look at the source fordiag.php:


```
root@carrier:/var/lib/lxd/containers/web/rootfs/var/www/html# cat diag.php
...[snip]...
                        <?php
                        $check = base64_decode($_POST["check"]);
                        if ($check) {
                            exec("ssh -i /var/www/.ssh/id_rsa root@10.99.64.2 'ps waux | grep " . $check . " | grep -v grep'", $output);
                            foreach($output as $line) {
                                echo "<p>" . $line . "</p>";
                            }
                        }
                        ?>
...[snip]...

```


As suspected, thecheckparameter is base64 decoded, and then used to build an ssh command string.
